## 2. Model Architecture

### Primary foundation: Wan VACE 14B

We have selected Wan VACE 14B as the initial generative video-editing foundation.

Research and verify its actual capabilities before implementing the inference pipeline.

Relevant resources:

- https://github.com/ali-vilab/VACE
- https://github.com/Wan-Video/Wan2.1
- https://huggingface.co/Wan-AI/Wan2.1-VACE-14B

### Supporting technologies

Evaluate:

- **SAM 2:** Video object segmentation and tracking.
- **PyTorch:** Model execution and eventual training.
- **Hugging Face Diffusers:** Inference integration where supported.
- **FFmpeg:** Video extraction, encoding, and processing.
- **ComfyUI:** Optional inference prototyping.
- **Gradio:** Initial user interface.

Prioritize native video editing rather than generating independent frames and stitching them together.

### Proposed processing pipeline

Original Video  
↓  
Object Selection  
↓  
SAM 2 Tracking and Mask Generation  
↓  
Text Prompt / Reference Image Conditioning  
↓  
Wan VACE 14B Video Editing  
↓  
Temporal Consistency Evaluation  
↓  
720p Video Export

Treat this as a proposed architecture, not a proven implementation. Verify compatibility and identify any missing components.

